  "summary": "Login and password-reset were unthrottled, so a scripted client could brute-force credentials or exhaust the email provider quota. This change adds a small token-bucket limiter backed by the existing Redis client and wires it into the two auth routes, returning `429` with a `Retry-After` header. The limiter is opt-in per route via a decorator, so the blast radius stays inside `auth/`.",
